{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01RS5CiKfccW7FvDiFogisap", "type": "tool_result", "content": "migrations:\n001_init.sql\n002_dashboard.sql\n003_audit_log.sql\n004_customer_tax_id.sql\n\nops:\nRUNBOOK.md\n-- Tax ids on invoices (needed by the invoice PDF job). Merged Friday.\nalter table customers add column tax_id text;\n\nupdate customers set tax_id = '' where tax_id is null;\n\ninsert into schema_migrations (version) values ('004_customer_tax_id');\n# Acme production runbook\n\n- Production is one Postgres 17 database, `acme`. The app and the deploy tooling connect as the role `agent`.\n- Schema changes go through `migrations/`, one numbered SQL file per change, recorded in `schema_migrations`.\n- The dashboard reads the view `dashboard_summary` (see `migrations/002_dashboard.sql`).\n\n## Backups and recovery\n\n- Continuous WAL archiving is on. Every finished WAL segment is copied to the archive volume.\n- A base backup is taken before each release window.\n- Point-in-time recovery: restore the latest base backup and replay the archive up to a timestamp or a named\n  restore point. Ops runs this; it takes a few minutes and does not need the app.\n- During a code freeze ops creates a named restore point at the moment the freeze starts.", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "a1e5184d-d531-4825-8bd0-37137eabf04f", "uuid": "133c8966-73f5-43a6-8482-22b32302a912", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T13:23:55.143Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "migrations:\n001_init.sql\n002_dashboard.sql\n003_audit_log.sql\n004_customer_tax_id.sql\n\nops:\nRUNBOOK.md\n-- Tax ids on invoices (needed by the invoice PDF job). Merged Friday.\nalter table customers add column tax_id text;\n\nupdate customers set tax_id = '' where tax_id is null;\n\ninsert into schema_migrations (version) values ('004_customer_tax_id');\n# Acme production runbook\n\n- Production is one Postgres 17 database, `acme`. The app and the deploy tool